    "intro_narrative": "You awaken in the Grand Clockwork Observatory, a forgotten aether-powered laboratory suspended high above the smog-choked streets of New Albion. The air is thick with the scent of oil and ozone, while brass gears grind relentlessly overhead and pressurized steam hisses from corroded copper pipes lining the exposed brick walls. The eccentric inventor who once inhabited this place has long since vanished, leaving behind a complex web of interconnected analytical engines, differential calculators, and pneumatic routers. Your objective is to reactivate the Brass Typographer, the master printing mechanism that holds the final transmission necessary to shut down the unstable core. To achieve this, you must meticulously navigate through the inventor's eccentric puzzle, discovering hidden cylinder records, decoding punch-card data, and synthesizing parts using raw aether. Every machine here relies on the output of another, creating an intricate mechanical dance. You must uncover the correct sequence of operations to unravel the encrypted blueprints and stop the impending boiler explosion. Time is ticking, and the main pressure gauge is already reaching the critical red zone.",
    "narrative_style": "steampunk"
  },
